{
  "schemaVersion": 1,
  "id": "kjv-psalms-068",
  "collection": "kjv-bible",
  "document_type": "bible_chapter",
  "number": 68,
  "title": "Psalms 68",
  "display_title": "Psalms 68",
  "translation": "King James Version",
  "translationCode": "KJV",
  "bookId": "psalms",
  "book": "Psalms",
  "bookName": "Psalms",
  "bookOrder": 19,
  "testament": "old",
  "chapter": 68,
  "sortOrder": 19068,
  "verseCount": 35,
  "aliases": [
    "Psalm",
    "Psalms",
    "Ps",
    "Psa",
    "Psm"
  ],
  "verses": [
    {
      "id": "verse-001",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 1,
      "verseId": "kjv:psalms:68:1",
      "numberLabel": "1",
      "text": "Let God arise, let his enemies be scattered: let them also that hate him flee before him.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Psalms 68:1",
        "verseKey": "kjv:psalms:68:1"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-002",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 2,
      "verseId": "kjv:psalms:68:2",
      "numberLabel": "2",
      "text": "As smoke is driven away, so drive them away: as wax melteth before the fire, so let the wicked perish at the presence of God.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Psalms 68:2",
        "verseKey": "kjv:psalms:68:2"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-003",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 3,
      "verseId": "kjv:psalms:68:3",
      "numberLabel": "3",
      "text": "But let the righteous be glad; let them rejoice before God: yea, let them exceedingly rejoice.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Psalms 68:3",
        "verseKey": "kjv:psalms:68:3"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-004",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 4,
      "verseId": "kjv:psalms:68:4",
      "numberLabel": "4",
      "text": "Sing unto God, sing praises to his name: extol him that rideth upon the heavens by his name JAH, and rejoice before him.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Psalms 68:4",
        "verseKey": "kjv:psalms:68:4"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-005",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 5,
      "verseId": "kjv:psalms:68:5",
      "numberLabel": "5",
      "text": "A father of the fatherless, and a judge of the widows, is God in his holy habitation.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Psalms 68:5",
        "verseKey": "kjv:psalms:68:5"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-006",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 6,
      "verseId": "kjv:psalms:68:6",
      "numberLabel": "6",
      "text": "God setteth the solitary in families: he bringeth out those which are bound with chains: but the rebellious dwell in a dry land.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Psalms 68:6",
        "verseKey": "kjv:psalms:68:6"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-007",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 7,
      "verseId": "kjv:psalms:68:7",
      "numberLabel": "7",
      "text": "O God, when thou wentest forth before thy people, when thou didst march through the wilderness; Selah:",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Psalms 68:7",
        "verseKey": "kjv:psalms:68:7"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-008",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 8,
      "verseId": "kjv:psalms:68:8",
      "numberLabel": "8",
      "text": "The earth shook, the heavens also dropped at the presence of God: even Sinai itself was moved at the presence of God, the God of Israel.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Psalms 68:8",
        "verseKey": "kjv:psalms:68:8"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-009",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 9,
      "verseId": "kjv:psalms:68:9",
      "numberLabel": "9",
      "text": "Thou, O God, didst send a plentiful rain, whereby thou didst confirm thine inheritance, when it was weary.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Psalms 68:9",
        "verseKey": "kjv:psalms:68:9"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-010",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 10,
      "verseId": "kjv:psalms:68:10",
      "numberLabel": "10",
      "text": "Thy congregation hath dwelt therein: thou, O God, hast prepared of thy goodness for the poor.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Psalms 68:10",
        "verseKey": "kjv:psalms:68:10"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-011",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 11,
      "verseId": "kjv:psalms:68:11",
      "numberLabel": "11",
      "text": "The Lord gave the word: great was the company of those that published it.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Psalms 68:11",
        "verseKey": "kjv:psalms:68:11"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-012",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 12,
      "verseId": "kjv:psalms:68:12",
      "numberLabel": "12",
      "text": "Kings of armies did flee apace: and she that tarried at home divided the spoil.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Psalms 68:12",
        "verseKey": "kjv:psalms:68:12"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-013",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 13,
      "verseId": "kjv:psalms:68:13",
      "numberLabel": "13",
      "text": "Though ye have lien among the pots, yet shall ye be as the wings of a dove covered with silver, and her feathers with yellow gold.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Psalms 68:13",
        "verseKey": "kjv:psalms:68:13"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-014",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 14,
      "verseId": "kjv:psalms:68:14",
      "numberLabel": "14",
      "text": "When the Almighty scattered kings in it, it was white as snow in Salmon.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Psalms 68:14",
        "verseKey": "kjv:psalms:68:14"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-015",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 15,
      "verseId": "kjv:psalms:68:15",
      "numberLabel": "15",
      "text": "The hill of God is as the hill of Bashan; an high hill as the hill of Bashan.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Psalms 68:15",
        "verseKey": "kjv:psalms:68:15"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-016",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 16,
      "verseId": "kjv:psalms:68:16",
      "numberLabel": "16",
      "text": "Why leap ye, ye high hills? this is the hill which God desireth to dwell in; yea, the LORD will dwell in it for ever.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Psalms 68:16",
        "verseKey": "kjv:psalms:68:16"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-017",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 17,
      "verseId": "kjv:psalms:68:17",
      "numberLabel": "17",
      "text": "The chariots of God are twenty thousand, even thousands of angels: the Lord is among them, as in Sinai, in the holy place.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Psalms 68:17",
        "verseKey": "kjv:psalms:68:17"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-018",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 18,
      "verseId": "kjv:psalms:68:18",
      "numberLabel": "18",
      "text": "Thou hast ascended on high, thou hast led captivity captive: thou hast received gifts for men; yea, for the rebellious also, that the LORD God might dwell among them.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Psalms 68:18",
        "verseKey": "kjv:psalms:68:18"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-019",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 19,
      "verseId": "kjv:psalms:68:19",
      "numberLabel": "19",
      "text": "Blessed be the Lord, who daily loadeth us with benefits, even the God of our salvation. Selah.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Psalms 68:19",
        "verseKey": "kjv:psalms:68:19"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-020",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 20,
      "verseId": "kjv:psalms:68:20",
      "numberLabel": "20",
      "text": "He that is our God is the God of salvation; and unto GOD the Lord belong the issues from death.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Psalms 68:20",
        "verseKey": "kjv:psalms:68:20"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-021",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 21,
      "verseId": "kjv:psalms:68:21",
      "numberLabel": "21",
      "text": "But God shall wound the head of his enemies, and the hairy scalp of such an one as goeth on still in his trespasses.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Psalms 68:21",
        "verseKey": "kjv:psalms:68:21"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-022",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 22,
      "verseId": "kjv:psalms:68:22",
      "numberLabel": "22",
      "text": "The Lord said, I will bring again from Bashan, I will bring my people again from the depths of the sea:",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Psalms 68:22",
        "verseKey": "kjv:psalms:68:22"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-023",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 23,
      "verseId": "kjv:psalms:68:23",
      "numberLabel": "23",
      "text": "That thy foot may be dipped in the blood of thine enemies, and the tongue of thy dogs in the same.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Psalms 68:23",
        "verseKey": "kjv:psalms:68:23"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-024",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 24,
      "verseId": "kjv:psalms:68:24",
      "numberLabel": "24",
      "text": "They have seen thy goings, O God; even the goings of my God, my King, in the sanctuary.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Psalms 68:24",
        "verseKey": "kjv:psalms:68:24"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-025",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 25,
      "verseId": "kjv:psalms:68:25",
      "numberLabel": "25",
      "text": "The singers went before, the players on instruments followed after; among them were the damsels playing with timbrels.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Psalms 68:25",
        "verseKey": "kjv:psalms:68:25"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-026",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 26,
      "verseId": "kjv:psalms:68:26",
      "numberLabel": "26",
      "text": "Bless ye God in the congregations, even the Lord, from the fountain of Israel.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Psalms 68:26",
        "verseKey": "kjv:psalms:68:26"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-027",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 27,
      "verseId": "kjv:psalms:68:27",
      "numberLabel": "27",
      "text": "There is little Benjamin with their ruler, the princes of Judah and their council, the princes of Zebulun, and the princes of Naphtali.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Psalms 68:27",
        "verseKey": "kjv:psalms:68:27"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-028",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 28,
      "verseId": "kjv:psalms:68:28",
      "numberLabel": "28",
      "text": "Thy God hath commanded thy strength: strengthen, O God, that which thou hast wrought for us.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Psalms 68:28",
        "verseKey": "kjv:psalms:68:28"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-029",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 29,
      "verseId": "kjv:psalms:68:29",
      "numberLabel": "29",
      "text": "Because of thy temple at Jerusalem shall kings bring presents unto thee.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Psalms 68:29",
        "verseKey": "kjv:psalms:68:29"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-030",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 30,
      "verseId": "kjv:psalms:68:30",
      "numberLabel": "30",
      "text": "Rebuke the company of spearmen, the multitude of the bulls, with the calves of the people, till every one submit himself with pieces of silver: scatter thou the people that delight in war.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Psalms 68:30",
        "verseKey": "kjv:psalms:68:30"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-031",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 31,
      "verseId": "kjv:psalms:68:31",
      "numberLabel": "31",
      "text": "Princes shall come out of Egypt; Ethiopia shall soon stretch out her hands unto God.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Psalms 68:31",
        "verseKey": "kjv:psalms:68:31"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-032",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 32,
      "verseId": "kjv:psalms:68:32",
      "numberLabel": "32",
      "text": "Sing unto God, ye kingdoms of the earth; O sing praises unto the Lord; Selah:",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Psalms 68:32",
        "verseKey": "kjv:psalms:68:32"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-033",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 33,
      "verseId": "kjv:psalms:68:33",
      "numberLabel": "33",
      "text": "To him that rideth upon the heavens of heavens, which were of old; lo, he doth send out his voice, and that a mighty voice.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Psalms 68:33",
        "verseKey": "kjv:psalms:68:33"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-034",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 34,
      "verseId": "kjv:psalms:68:34",
      "numberLabel": "34",
      "text": "Ascribe ye strength unto God: his excellency is over Israel, and his strength is in the clouds.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Psalms 68:34",
        "verseKey": "kjv:psalms:68:34"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-035",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 35,
      "verseId": "kjv:psalms:68:35",
      "numberLabel": "35",
      "text": "O God, thou art terrible out of thy holy places: the God of Israel is he that giveth strength and power unto his people. Blessed be God.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Psalms 68:35",
        "verseKey": "kjv:psalms:68:35"
      }
    }
  ],
  "source": {
